# GraphQL schema for the `mlc` bounded context.
#
# Schema-first: this file is the contract, and the resolver signatures are checked against it
# at startup. Per adr/0020-graphql-as-the-only-transport.adr.md, GraphQL is the *only*
# transport in the MVP — so this file is not one representation of the API, it is the API, and
# renaming a field here is a breaking change for the Backoffice UI.
#
# `extend type Mutation` rather than `type Mutation`: the root is declared once, in
# booking.graphqls, and graphql-java rejects a duplicate type definition. Every context adds
# its operations by extension.
#
# No `Query` field. The GraphQL specification requires a schema to declare a Query root and
# booking.graphqls already does; this service still has no read side, and adding a domain query
# needs the read-side ADR that is not written yet.
#
# SDD: see documentation/use-cases/uc07-create-master-leasing-contract.spec.md § 9.

extend type Mutation {
    "UC07 — create a master leasing contract (Leasingrahmenvertrag) with the first version of its terms."
    createMasterLeasingContract(input: CreateMasterLeasingContractInput!): CreateMasterLeasingContractPayload!
}

# The six non-null fields are exactly the ones PD-01 makes mandatory — a provisional decision
# of ours, not a sourced rule. The JCM data model page lists every field and states no
# optionality anywhere.
#
# Monetary and percentage values are `String` and not `Float`: GraphQL's Float is a
# double-precision binary float and cannot represent money exactly. This service declares no
# decimal scalar, so decimal notation on the wire is the honest option — the booking context
# carries its date as a String for the same reason.
#
# There is deliberately NO timestamp field. architecture.definition.md § 8.1 puts a GraphQL
# client in the same category as a REST client: the moment an action happened is the system's
# observation, not the caller's claim (PD-11). Both `creationTime` and `activationDate` are
# read from ClockPort (PD-08).
input CreateMasterLeasingContractInput {
    "Reference to the employer this framework agreement is established with (Arbeitgeber)."
    employerId: String!
    "Reference to the lessor party (Leasinggeber)."
    lessorId: String!
    "Join key between Odoo and Radar (Partnernummer). Omit when not yet known."
    partnerNumber: String
    "The internal team owning this record. Not the acting user — this service has no authentication."
    owner: String

    "Maximum credit exposure allowed on this contract. Decimal notation, e.g. \"50000.00\"."
    creditLimit: String!
    "The commercial model the contract runs under, e.g. \"salary-sacrifice-leasing\"."
    contractType: String!
    "ISO-4217 alphabetic code, e.g. \"EUR\"."
    currency: String!
    "Number of employees entitled to lease under this contract (JobRad-Berechtigte)."
    eligibleEmployees: Int!

    "The channel or segment through which the contract was sold."
    salesChannel: String
    "Whether this contract shares joint liability with other companies in its corporate group. Defaults to false."
    groupJointLiability: Boolean
    "Share of active leases per year dissolvable without penalty (Rückgabekontingent). Decimal, 0–100."
    returnQuotaPercentage: String
    "Fee owed if the return quota is claimed within the early-claim window. Decimal, 0–100."
    earlyClaimFeePercentage: String
    "Months within which claiming the quota counts as early."
    earlyClaimWindowMonths: Int
    "How much notice either party must give to terminate (Kündigungsfrist)."
    noticePeriodRule: String
    "Code identifying the agreed payment terms."
    paymentTerms: String
    "Lowest bike price this contract permits leasing. Decimal. Supply with priceRangeMax or not at all."
    priceRangeMin: String
    "Highest bike price this contract permits leasing. Decimal. Supply with priceRangeMin or not at all."
    priceRangeMax: String
    "How the leasing price is derived from sale price and shipping cost."
    calculationBasis: String
    "Service tiers employees may choose from (Servicepakete). Defaults to empty."
    servicePackageOptions: [String!]
    "Version of the service-package terms, tracked separately from the contract version."
    servicePackageVersion: Int
    "Whether the employer can edit bike categories in the manager portal. Defaults to false."
    categoriesEditableInPortal: Boolean
}

# Derived, not sourced: no source specifies a response shape. § 3 derives these four from what
# the caller cannot otherwise learn — this service has no read side, so a caller not told the
# identifiers has no second way to obtain them.
type CreateMasterLeasingContractPayload {
    masterLeasingContractId: ID!
    "ACTIVE on creation (PD-07)."
    status: String!
    "Identity of the terms version created with the contract — the source's mlc_config_id."
    configurationId: ID!
    "Always 1 on creation."
    configurationVersion: Int!
}
